  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Montana received $1.1B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The state recorded 7,266 awards with an average award size of $151K. Obligations are down 4.1% year over year. All figures are contract obligations and current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date). The Department of Defense obligated $338M, the Department of Agriculture obligated $295M, and the Department of Homeland Security obligated $173M in Montana during the same period. Nonscheduled Chartered Freight Air Transportation is the largest industry by obligations at $177M, followed by Electronic and Precision Equipment Repair and Maintenance at $137M and Commercial and Institutional Building Construction at $129M. S & K SECURITY GROUP LLC is the top vendor with $135M, with BRIDGER AIR TANKER LLC and ARCHER WESTERN FEDERAL JV next at $62.4M and $58.9M respectively. Year-to-year obligations moved from $691M in FY21 to $925M in FY22, $1B in FY23, and $1.1B in FY24, FY25, and FY26 to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies drive federal contracting in Montana?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the largest buying agency with $338M in obligations. The Department of Agriculture follows with $295M, and the Department of Homeland Security follows with $173M. The Department of the Interior, Department of Transportation, and Department of Health and Human Services also appear among the top buyers with $93.4M, $79.5M, and $57.4M respectively."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who captures the most federal contract dollars in Montana?",
        "body": "S & K SECURITY GROUP LLC tops the vendor list with $135M in obligations. BRIDGER AIR TANKER LLC and ARCHER WESTERN FEDERAL JV follow with $62.4M and $58.9M. Construction and air services vendors appear frequently among the top recipients, including PAF ELECTRICAL, INC. at $57M and S & K AEROSPACE, LLC at $41.9M."
      }
    ]
  },
